{"strongs": "H8548", "word": "תָּמִיד", "translit": "ta.mid", "root": "מוד", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "continuity", "definition": "תָּמִיד noun masculine Dan 12:11 continuity (perhaps originally extent ; Late Hebrew as Biblical Hebrew, Ecclus תמיד Eccl 45:14 ); — ׳ ת always absolute; — 1. earliest and oftenest as adverb, continually: \\ \\ a. of going on without interruption = continuously , Hos 12:7 ; Jer 6:7 ; Nah 3:19 ; Isa 21:8 ; Isa 49:16 ; Isa 51:13 (+ כָּלהַֿיּוֺם ), Isa 52:5 (+ id. ), Isa 60:11 (|| יַוֺמָם וָלַיְלָח , Isa 62:6 (+ כָּלהַֿיּוֺם וְכָלהַֿלַּיְלָה ), Isa 65:3 ; Obad 1:16 ; Hab 1:17 ; Deut 11:12 ; 1Kgs 10:8 = 2Chr 9:7 ; 1Chr 16:11 ; 1Chr 16:37 especially (sometimes hyperbole) in Psalms : Ps 16:8 ; Ps 25:15 ; Ps 34:2 (|| בְּכָלעֵֿת ), Ps 35:27 compare Ps 40:17 ; Ps 70:5 ; Ps 38:18 ; Ps 40:12 ; Ps 50:8 ; Ps 51:5 ; Ps 69:24 ; Ps 71:6 ; Ps 71:14 ; Ps 72:15 ; Ps 73:23 ; Ps 74:23 ; Ps 105:4 ; Ps 109:15 ; Ps 109:19 ; Ps 119:44 (+ וֶָעך׃ לְעוֺלָם ), v Ps 40:109 ; (so also Ps 16:5 , for ᵑ0 תומי , Bi Che ; תּוֺסיף Ol Bae ); Prov 5:19 (|| בִּכָלעֵֿת ), Prov 6:21 ; Prov 15:15 ; Prov 28:14 also Ezek 38:8 (strike out ᵑ6 Co Toy Hpt. Berthol ), Lev 6:6 ( P ; of fire, || לֹא תִכְבֶּה ), and Lev 46:14 (but ׳ חֻקַּת תּ ᵐ5 Co Berthol ); also in ritual, Lev 24:8 ( H ), compare Exod 25:30 ( P ; shew-bread), Lev 24:2 ; Lev 24:3 ; Lev 24:4 ( H ), compare Exod 27:20 ( P ; of lamp), Exod 28:29 ; Exod 28:30 ; Exod 28:38 . \\ \\ b. of regular repetition: meals 2Sam 9:7 ; 2Sam 9:10 ; 2Sam 9:13 ; 2Kgs 25:29 = Jer 52:33 journeys 2Kgs 4:19 compare Num 9:16 ; Ps 71:3 of ritual: sacrifice, לַיּוֺם תָּמִיד Exod 29:38 compare 1Chr 16:40 ; 1Chr 23:31 ; 2Chr 24:14 . 2. as substantive: \\ \\ a. of uninterrupted continuity, ׳ אַנְשֵׁי ת Ezek 39:14 men of continuity , i.e. men continually employed for the purpose; ׳ לֶחֶם הַתּ Num 4:7 the bread of continuity , i.e. the bread that is always there, so ׳ מַעֲרֶכֶת ת 2Chr 2:3 , and perhaps ׳ חֲצֹצְרוֺת ת 1Chr 16:6 . \\ \\ b. of regular repetition ׳ אֲרֻחַת מ 2Kgs 25:30 , i.e. a regular allowance, = Jer 52:34 especially of ritual: ׳ קְטֹרֶת ת Exod 30:8 ( P ); most often ׳ עֹלַת ת Ezek 46:15 (every morning), Exod 29:42 (morning and evening, so) Num 28:6 ; Ezra 3:5 , so read also Num 28:3 ( Di ) for ᵑ0 ׳ עוֺלָה ת ( לַיּוֺם ); ׳ עֹלַת הַת Num 28:10 ; Num 28:15 ; Num 28:23 ; Num 28:24 ; Num 28:31 ; Num 29:6 ; Num 29:11 ; Num 29:16 ; Num 29:19 ; Num 29:22 ; Num 29:25 ; Num 29:28 ; Num 29:31 ; Num 29:34 ; Num 29:38 Neh Neh 10:35 rarely ׳ מִנְחַת ת Num 4:16 ( P ), Neh 10:34 as appositive, ׳ מִנְחָה ת Lev 6:13 meal-offering as a regular observance (compare Ges «GKC:131»§ 131 , 2 (b) Da Synt.§ 29 (b); on text see Di , Now Archaeology ii. 124 f. ), (and Num 28:3 ᵑ0 , but see above) \\ \\ c. (late) ׳ הַת alone = daily (morning and evening) burnt-offering ( Now Archaeology ii. 222 f. ) Dan 8:11 ; Dan 8:12 ; Dan 8:13 ; Dan 11:31 ; Dan 12:11 (so Talmud, even in plural תְּמִידִין ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4540')\">BDB4540</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8548')\">H8548</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4539')\">BDB4539</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4541')\">BDB4541</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>תָּמִיד</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Dan 12:11\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(27,12,11)\">Dan 12:11</ref></sup> <highlightword>continuity</highlightword> (perhaps originally <highlight>extent</highlight>; Late Hebrew as Biblical Hebrew, Ecclus <bdbheb>תמיד</bdbheb> <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Eccl 45:14\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(21,45,14)\">Eccl 45:14</ref>); — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ת</bdbheb> always absolute; — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> earliest and oftenest as adverb, <highlight>continually:</highlight> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> of going on without interruption = <highlight>continuously</highlig